{"path":"experimental/ranges/functional/less_equal","title":"std::experimental::ranges::less_equal","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::ranges::</span>less_equal","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/less_equal","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"Function object for performing comparisons. The primary template invokes operator< on const lvalues of type T with the argument order inverted and then negates the result.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/experimental/ranges/functional\">&lt;experimental/ranges/functional&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-ranges\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"kw4\">void</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; requires StrictTotallyOrdered<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">||</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Same<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, <span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">||</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<span class=\"coMULTI\">/* &lt; on two const T lvalues invokes a built-in operator comparing pointers */</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> less_equal<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-ranges-ts t-mark-ts\">(ranges TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-ranges\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> less_equal<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-ranges-ts t-mark-ts\">(ranges TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Function object for performing comparisons. The primary template invokes <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">operator<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span></span></code> on const lvalues of type <code>T</code> with the argument order inverted and then negates the result. The specialization <code>less_equal&lt;void&gt;</code> deduces the parameter types of the function call operator from the arguments (but not the return type).\n</p><p>All specializations of <code>less_equal</code> are <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/concepts/Semiregular\"><code>Semiregular</code></a>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Member_types\">Member types</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-hitem\">\n<td> Member type\n</td>\n<td> Definition\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code>is_transparent</code> <span class=\"t-mark\">(member only of <code>less_equal&lt;void&gt;</code> specialization)</span>\n</td>\n<td> /* unspecified */\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Member_functions\">Member functions</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator()</span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  checks if the first argument is <i>less</i> than or <i>equal</i> to the second <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<div class=\"t-member\">\n<h2 id=\"std::experimental::ranges::less_equal::operator.28.29\"><span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::ranges::less_equal::</span>operator()</h2>\n<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> operator<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> x, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> y<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark\">(member only of primary <code>less_equal&lt;T&gt;</code> template)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> U <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; requires StrictTotallyOrderedWith<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">||</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<span class=\"coMULTI\">/* std::declval&lt;T&gt;() &lt; std::declval&lt;U&gt;() resolves to<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; a built-in operator comparing pointers */</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> operator<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> t, U<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> u<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark\">(member only of <code>less_equal&lt;void&gt;</code> specialization)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Compares <code>x</code> and <code>y</code>. Equivalent to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/less\"><span class=\"kw2862\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">less</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>y, x<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Compares <code>t</code> and <code>u</code>. Equivalent to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/less\"><span class=\"kw2862\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">less</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/forward\"><span class=\"kw1125\">std::<span class=\"me2\">forward</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>u<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/forward\"><span class=\"kw1125\">std::<span class=\"me2\">forward</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>t<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>.\n</div></div>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Unlike <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/less_equal\">std::less_equal</a></span>, <code>ranges::less_equal</code> requires all six comparison operators <code>&lt;</code>, <code>&lt;=</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>&gt;=</code>, <code>==</code> and <code>!=</code> to be valid (via the <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/concepts/StrictTotallyOrdered\"><code>StrictTotallyOrdered</code></a> and <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/concepts/StrictTotallyOrdered\"><code>StrictTotallyOrderedWith</code></a> constraints) and is entirely defined in terms of <span class=\"t-lc\">ranges::less</span>. However, the implementation is free to use <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">operator<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;=</span></span></code> directly, because those concepts require the results of the comparison operators to be consistent.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/less_equal\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>less_equal</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  function object implementing <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;=</span> y</span></code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Member types","id":"Member_types"},{"depth":3,"text":"Member functions","id":"Member_functions"},{"depth":2,"text":"std::experimental::ranges::less_equal::operator()","id":"std::experimental::ranges::less_equal::operator.28.29"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/ranges","title":"Extensions for ranges"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::ranges::less_equal","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. Function object for performing comparisons."},{"label":"Member types","children":[{"label":"is_transparent (member only of less_equal<void>…","note":"/* unspecified */"}]},{"label":"Member functions","children":[{"label":"operator()","note":"checks if the first argument is less than or equal to the second"}]},{"label":"std::experimental::ranges::less_equal::operator()","note":"Compares x and y. Equivalent to return !ranges::less<>{}(y, x);.","children":[{"label":"